<h2 class="story-title">Chouboli's Struggle - Breaking Point</h2>

"The thief was clearly—"  
"No, the SETH—"  
"But the thakur's transformation—"

They're going in circles. Deliberately. Mockingly. Neither will acknowledge the OBVIOUS truth.

Chouboli trembles with fury. Every fiber of her being screams to correct them. Her head pounds. Her vision blurs with rage.

<div class="struggle-box3">
**Chouboli's thoughts:**

*ENOUGH. They're fools. BOTH of them. The sethani stood in that room, dressed for betrayal, and chose TRUTH over safety. She's the one most true, and someone needs to SAY IT. I can't— I CAN'T hold this in anymore—*
</div>

The words are at her lips. The oath is shattering.

**Chouboli can barely contain herself:**

